            {"t": "p", "c": "The centre of a picture should sit at eye level when you are standing — roughly 145–150cm from the floor. Above sofas, the bottom edge should clear the back of the sofa by about 15–20cm. Art floats when it hangs like a museum plaque."},
            {"t": "h2", "c": "4. Fighting the light instead of using it"},
            {"t": "p", "c": "Choosing dark, moody walls for a north-facing room, or a single overhead light with no dimmer, are both ways of losing a battle with the room’s natural condition. Design with the light you have before you add more of it."},
