            {"t": "p", "c": "When a room doesn’t feel right, the instinct is to add another object. It is usually the wrong instinct. Remove first — a layer of objects, a busy rug, a duplicated lamp — and see what the room was trying to be. Most rooms improve more from subtraction than from addition."},
